<title>UK: Cerinvest adds 40 mln euros to Dec 2002 bond.</title>
<headline>Cerinvest adds 40 mln euros to Dec 2002 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 100 million euros from 60 million euros, joint lead managers Banque Internationale a Luxembourg and Cera Bank said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CERINVEST NV</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  CERA BANK (RATED A1)</p>
<p> AMT   100 MLN EURO   COUPON     5.50	MATURITY    06.DEC.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.25    PAY DATE  S-06.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     SPREAD    +15 BP OVER THE CURVE</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 1-10	SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC   1.75</p>
<p> NOTES     *PAID IN ECU AT RATE OF ONE ECU PER ONE EURO UNTIL</p>
<p>		THE EURO IS INTRODUCED IN THE THIRD STAGE OF EMU.</p>
<p>		S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>		ORIGINAL 60 MLN EURO LAUNCHED 09.APR.97</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
